<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tōtōmi Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tōtōmi Province was an old province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in the western part of present-day Shizuoka Prefecture, around Lake Hamana. Long ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imagawa-clan">Imagawa clan</a>, it was contested after 1560 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takeda-shingen">Takeda Shingen</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a>, who took most of it and moved his base to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamamatsu">Hamamatsu</a> in 1570. Shingen defeated Ieyasu there at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mikatagahara">Battle of Mikatagahara</a> in 1573.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/totomi-province.jpg" alt="Tōtōmi Province" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ash_Crow · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Provinces_of_Japan-Totomi.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
